Here are the essential sections you need to effectively showcase a multidisciplinary portfolio:
## 1. The Hero Section (The Hook)
This is the first thing people see before they scroll. It needs to instantly communicate your range and grab attention.
 * **The Identity:** Introduce yourself clearly. You can use your real name, Pruthvi, and optionally introduce your pen name, DeVenLucaz, to bridge your technical and creative personas.
 * **The Tagline:** A punchy one-liner that captures your duality. Something that highlights your background as a mechanical engineer alongside your digital creation.
 * **The Call to Action (CTA):** A primary button that directs visitors immediately to your best work (e.g., "See My Games" or "Explore Projects").
## 2. The Project Portfolio (The Proof)
Because you build across very different domains, you need to categorize your work so visitors can navigate it easily without getting overwhelmed.
 * **Software & AI:** Highlight your technical tools. For a project like *llamdrop*, include a brief explainer of what it achieves (like running local LLMs on Android), the environment you use (Termux), and a direct link to the GitHub repository.
 * **Game Development:** Games are visual, so this section needs imagery. Feature the logos and screenshots for your titles like *Elyra*, *Minepath*, and *Word Heist*, along with brief descriptions of the game mechanics.
 * **Creative Writing & Lore:** Give your narrative work its own dedicated space. For *DAAYAN - Bandhan*, include a compelling synopsis, thematic elements like the mythology, and emphasize the core friendship between the main characters.
## 3. The "About the Creator" Section (The Story)
People connect with the person behind the projects. This is where you explain *how* you do what you do.
 * **Your Workflow:** Explicitly mention that you are a vibe coder. Explaining how you orchestrate different AI models to execute technical syntax based on your high-level vision is a fascinating modern workflow that stands out.
 * **Your Background:** Briefly touch on your mechanical engineering roots and how that structural, problem-solving mindset translates into game logic and app development.
 * **Languages:** Mention your multilingual fluency (Hindi, Marathi, English) and your ear for register shifting. It’s a massive asset for character dialogue in your writing and localization in your games.
## 4. The Footer & Contact (The Connection)
Keep this functional and easy to find at the bottom of the page.
 * **Professional Links:** Your GitHub profile and any relevant developer community handles.
 * **Direct Contact:** A simple mailto link or contact form for collaborations, along with any social platforms where you actively share your work.
